{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hybrid cloud hybrid cloud","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","fileName":"Hybrid Cloud.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hybrid Cloud","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Service and Deployment Models]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Service and Deployment Models","Private Cloud","Cloud Bursting","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hybrid cloud hybrid cloud","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","fileName":"Hybrid Cloud.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hybrid Cloud","heading":"Hybrid Cloud","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A hybrid cloud combines two or more component clouds into a system with its own useful characteristics. The components may use public, private, or community deployment models and may expose different service abstraction levels.\n\nThe components normally need to share data, processes, or control. A hybrid design can keep sensitive work in a [[Private Cloud]] while using standard public services for flexibility, or can duplicate a service in another cloud for continuity and [[Cloud Bursting]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Service and Deployment Models","Private Cloud","Cloud Bursting","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hybrid cloud hybrid cloud","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hybrid Cloud.md","file